# Sidekick – AI Medical Appointment Assistant

A real-time AI-powered web app that listens to doctor–patient conversations, simplifies medical terminology, suggests clarification questions, generates visit summaries, and optionally translates into the patient's language.

---

## 1. System Architecture

```mermaid
graph TD
    subgraph Browser ["Browser (Frontend)"]
        MIC[🎤 Microphone Input]
        UI[Real-Time UI Panel]
        SUM[Visit Summary View]
    end

    subgraph Server ["FastAPI Backend"]
        WS[WebSocket Handler]
        STT[Speech-to-Text<br/>Web Speech API]
        LLM[LLM Engine<br/>Google Gemini API]
        DB[(SQLite Database)]
    end

    MIC -->|Audio stream / text| WS
    WS -->|Transcript chunks| LLM
    LLM -->|Simplified terms<br/>Questions<br/>Translations| WS
    WS -->|Real-time updates| UI
    WS -->|End session| SUM
    LLM -->|Summary| DB
    WS -->|Save transcript| DB
```

### How it works
1. **Browser captures speech** via the Web Speech API (SpeechRecognition) — no server-side STT needed.
2. **Transcript chunks** are sent over a WebSocket to the FastAPI backend.
3. **Backend calls Google Gemini** (free tier) to simplify medical terms, suggest questions, and optionally translate.
4. **Results stream back** via WebSocket to the frontend in real time.
5. At session end, a **structured visit summary** is generated and stored in SQLite.

> [!NOTE]
> Speech recognition runs entirely in the browser (Web Speech API), keeping the backend lightweight. The Gemini API free tier provides 15 RPM / 1M tokens per day — more than enough for an MVP demo.

---

## 2. Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology | Rationale |
|-------|-----------|-----------|
| **Frontend** | Vanilla HTML + CSS + JS | Zero build step, fast iteration |
| **Speech-to-Text** | Web Speech API (`SpeechRecognition`) | Built into Chrome/Edge, free, real-time |
| **Backend** | Python + FastAPI | Async, WebSocket-native, fast to develop |
| **AI / LLM** | Google Gemini API (gemini-2.0-flash) | Free tier, excellent medical understanding |
| **Database** | SQLite via `aiosqlite` | Zero setup, file-based, perfect for MVP |
| **Translation** | Gemini (same LLM call) | One model handles simplification + translation |
| **Deployment** | Local (uvicorn) | Simple, no cloud costs |

